# A missing build asset is a 404, never the app shell. Only a stale tab asks
# for one — an old deploy's chunk name — and without this line the catch-all
# below answered it with index.html and a 200, which `_headers` then told the
# browser to keep for a year under a JavaScript URL. Not forced (no `!`), so
# every asset that exists is still served first.
/assets/*  /404.html  404

# The SPA fallback. Deliberately NOT forced: Netlify serves an existing file in
# preference to a non-forced rule, which is what lets the prerendered link
# preview pages (G6) exist at all. See CLAUDE.md, "Link previews (G6)".
/*    /index.html   200
